.TH RUFUSARM64-CLI 1 "28 July 2026" "RufusArm64 0.15.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rufusarm64-cli \- inspect images and safely create bootable USB media on Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rufusarm64-cli list
.RI [ --all ]
.RI [ --json ]
.PP
.B rufusarm64-cli inspect
.BI --image " FILE"
.RI [ --json ]
.PP
.B rufusarm64-cli hash
.RI [ --algorithm " md5|sha1|sha256|sha512" ]
.RI [ --all ]
.RI [ --json ]
.I FILE
.PP
.B sudo rufusarm64-cli write
.BI --image " FILE"
.BI --device " /dev/DEVICE"
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B rufusarm64-cli acquire
.RI "verify|list|download|channel list|channel download"
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B rufusarm64-cli dbx
.RI "inspect|update|check|scan"
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B rufusarm64-cli uefi
.RI "validate|integrity manifest|integrity verify"
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B rufusarm64-cli uefi-ntfs inspect
.RI [ --image " FILE" ]
.RI [ --json ]
.PP
.B rufusarm64-cli persistence
.RI "plan|analyze"
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B sudo rufusarm64-cli qualify
.RI "start|verify"
.RI [ options ]
.B rufusarm64-cli update verify --root FILE [--root FILE...] --release FILE [--current-version VERSION] [--minimum-metadata-version N] [--state-file FILE] [--json]
.br
.B rufusarm64-cli update refresh [--config FILE] [--cache-dir DIR] [--state-file FILE] [--current-version VERSION] [--minimum-metadata-version N] [--offline] [--json]
.br
.B rufusarm64-cli update download --root FILE [--root FILE...] --release FILE [--current-version VERSION] [--minimum-metadata-version N] [--state-file FILE] [--output FILE] [--replace] [--resume] [--json-progress|--json]
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rufusarm64-cli
is the native helper and troubleshooting interface used by RufusArm64. It
writes recognized GPT/MBR disk images and Linux ISOHybrid media directly,
prepares supported compressed and virtual-disk inputs, and creates extracted
Windows installation media using GPT or MBR, UEFI or x86-family BIOS/CSM, and
Automatic, FAT32, or NTFS selection.
.PP
The graphical application supplies exact source and target identities, guarded
cancellation, and fresh Polkit authorization. Direct terminal use must retain
the same safety boundary and verify the exact whole-disk path before writing.
.SH IMAGE INSPECTION AND CHECKSUMS
.B list
returns eligible whole devices and identity tokens. The default view excludes
ordinary fixed disks and the running system disk.
.PP
.B inspect
performs read-only recognition of supported image and container formats. JSON
output remains available when an unusable image produces a nonzero status.
.PP
.B hash
reads one identity-bound regular-file descriptor. With no options it computes
SHA-256. Use repeated
.B --algorithm
or
.B --all
to calculate the ordered MD5, SHA-1, SHA-256, and SHA-512 comparison set. MD5
and SHA-1 are legacy comparison values only and are never used for acquisition
trust or destructive-write assurance.
.SH COMMON WRITE OPTIONS
.TP
.B --verify
Flush block buffers and compare copied data after writing. Recommended.
.TP
.BI --partition-scheme " gpt|mbr"
Choose the Windows-media partition table. GPT is the default.
.TP
.BI --target-system " uefi|bios"
Choose UEFI or legacy BIOS/UEFI-CSM. Windows ARM64 is UEFI-only.
.TP
.BI --filesystem " auto|fat32|ntfs"
Choose the Windows-media filesystem. Automatic prefers FAT32 when safe and
otherwise selects NTFS. FAT32 can split oversized WIM or ESD payloads.
.TP
.BI --cluster-size " SIZE"
Select a supported Windows filesystem allocation unit.
.TP
.BI --label " LABEL"
Set the validated target volume label where the selected mode supports it.
.TP
.BI --driver-folder " DIRECTORY"
Validate and stage Windows driver packages for Windows PE and manual Setup use.
.TP
.BI --dbx-file " FILE"
Reject Windows EFI boot files revoked by the selected Secure Boot DBX. Firmware
is not modified.
.TP
.B --win-silent-install
Create guarded Windows 11 unattended media that may erase disk 0 on the
installation computer. This requires qualified UEFI/NTFS media, an exact image
index, a local account, privacy choices, locale, time zone, no pre-existing
answer file, and the independent acknowledgement below. Disconnect all other
storage before booting the result.
.TP
.BI --win-install-image-index " INDEX"
Select the exact WIM image index proven by the current ISO inspection. Display
names are not accepted as substitutes for an index.
.TP
.BI --win-silent-confirm " PHRASE"
For silent installation, require the exact literal phrase
.BR "ERASE DISK 0" .
This is separate from
.B --yes
and does not bypass source, target, media, layout, or answer-file checks.
.TP
.B --full-format
Zero-write the new Windows data partition before formatting.
.TP
.B --bad-block-check
Zero-write and read back the complete new Windows data partition before format.
.TP
.BI --expected-identity " TOKEN"
Require the refreshed target identity returned by
.BR "rufusarm64-cli list --json" .
The graphical workflows always supply this value.
.TP
.B --yes
Skip terminal confirmation. This never bypasses identity or target-policy
checks and is intended for reviewed automation.
.TP
.B --allow-fixed
Permit an explicitly selected non-removable whole disk for direct terminal use.
The running system disk and protected mounts remain refused. Graphical paths do
not expose this option.
.TP
.B --no-unmount
Refuse mounted descendants rather than unmounting eligible removable media.

.SH EXPERIMENTAL WINDOWS TO GO
The explicit
.B --mode windows-to-go
path accepts only positively identified Windows 11 client ARM64 media and a
reviewed GPT/UEFI/NTFS target. It creates a 260 MiB unlabelled FAT32 EFI System
Partition, applies the exact selected WIM image directly to the unmounted NTFS
partition, builds BCD transactionally from the image's own BCD-Template, binds
the exact disk and partition GUIDs, disables recovery, installs the ARM64
fallback loader, writes offline SAN policy 4, and independently reopens both
filesystems read-only for verification.
.PP
The mode requires
.B --experimental-windows-to-go,
.BI --win-to-go-image-index " INDEX",
and the exact acknowledgement
.BR "--win-to-go-confirm 'CREATE EXPERIMENTAL WINDOWS TO GO'" .
It accepts optional first-boot flags for online-account bypass, a local
administrator, reduced data collection, Quality of Life changes, and
locale/time-zone settings. The exact combined Windows/Panther/unattend.xml is
size/SHA-256 bound before erasure and read back after creation; SAN policy 4 is
mandatory and keeps internal disks offline. It refuses hardware-check bypass,
silent installation, BitLocker suppression, SkuSiPolicy, CA 2023 replacement,
driver staging, DBX overrides, manual filesystem/layout choices, unsupported
architecture, insufficient expanded capacity, changed sources or targets, and
mounted/protected targets.
.PP
Microsoft removed Windows To Go from supported modern Windows releases. The
result remains experimental: software and loop-device verification do not prove
physical firmware boot or successful first boot. Encrypted-file restoration and
Windows extended attributes remain upstream wimlib limitations.
.SH LINUX PERSISTENCE
.B persistence plan
analyzes a caller-mounted media tree without opening a target device.
.B persistence analyze
mounts the exact identity-bound source image read-only and returns the same
bounded plan used by creation.
.PP
The guarded creator supports a narrow Ubuntu casper and Debian live-boot
contract: a fresh GPT, writable FAT32 boot partition, ext4 persistence
partition, architecture-matching fallback UEFI loader, FAT32-safe media tree,
and at least 1 GiB of persistence capacity. Unsupported boot layouts, unsafe
links, oversized FAT32 files, compressed inputs, encrypted persistence, and
MBR/BIOS persistence are refused.
.PP
The direct writer requires both
.B --mode linux-persistent
and
.B --experimental-persistence .
The installed graphical workflow uses its separate package-owned helper.
.PP
.B qualify start
and
.B qualify verify
record an observed boot and later reboot of the same persistent USB. Passing
qualification proves only the exact image, USB, controller, firmware, and
computer that were observed.
.SH SIGNED IMAGE ACQUISITION
Local acquisition commands validate detached Ed25519-signed catalogues.
Built-in channel commands use package-owned threshold-root metadata, monotonic
rollback protection, expiry checks, verified cache fallback, HTTPS and redirect
host restrictions, exact size, SHA-256, storage-space preflight, and atomic
installation.
.PP
Resumable mode retains only an owner-private partial bound to the signed image
identity and rehashes it before reuse. Cancellation or failure never installs
an unverified image. The production built-in channel remains disabled until
reviewed public mirrors and offline trust metadata are provisioned.
.SH VERIFIED RELEASE UPDATES
.B update verify
validates a threshold-signed release envelope through a supplied sequential root
chain. It binds the release version, tag, commit, channel, exact asset names,
sizes, SHA-256 digests, GitHub release URLs, and authorized signing key IDs.
The command refuses expired metadata, root-version or root-content rollback,
release-metadata version or content rollback, release-version rollback, and a
system clock more than 24 hours behind the last accepted metadata time. On every
successful verification it advances an owner-only rollback record under
`$XDG_STATE_HOME/rufusarm64/update/state.json`, or
`$HOME/.local/state/rufusarm64/update/state.json` when XDG_STATE_HOME is unset.
.B --state-file
selects an explicit path. The state directory is secured to mode 0700; the state
and lock files use mode 0600, no-follow admission, single-link ownership checks,
an exclusive process lock, atomic replacement, and directory synchronization.
.B --minimum-metadata-version
is an additional operator floor and cannot lower the persisted floor.
.PP
.B update refresh
loads a package-owned pinned metadata-channel configuration, replays the cached
root chain from the packaged bootstrap root, fetches sequential root rotations
and the threshold-signed release envelope, and commits acceptance through the
same rollback state used by local verification. The optional
.B release_url
uses the configured HTTPS host allowlist and the existing TLS 1.2+, redirect,
compression, and byte-limit policy. Verified metadata is cached under the user
cache directory with mode 0700 directories and mode 0600 files.
.B --offline
uses only an unexpired independently reverified cache. Network errors may fall
back to that cache, but signature, expiry, rollback, substitution, and clock
failures do not. Refresh and acceptance are bound to the same state path; the
state and lock must remain outside the metadata cache and cannot overwrite the
packaged configuration or bootstrap root. No package is downloaded or installed.
.PP
.B update download
requires the same authenticated metadata and additionally requires the signed
release to be newer than the current version. It uses the bounded acquisition
writer to enforce signed URL and redirect hosts, exact byte count, SHA-256,
resumable partial identity, cancellation, available-space checks, atomic
no-replace publication, directory synchronization, and verified reuse of an
existing destination. It downloads only the exact ARM64 Debian package bound by
the signed release metadata. It does not request privilege or install software.

.SH SECURE BOOT DBX
.B dbx inspect
parses one bounded, stable, non-empty regular file or the exact running firmware
DBX variable. It reports direct SHA-256 and exact X.509 certificate revocations
without modifying firmware.
.PP
.B dbx update
supports x86, amd64, ARM, and ARM64. It downloads from one reviewed immutable
commit in Microsoft's public secureboot_objects repository and verifies the
exact Git blob object identity before parsing, creating a cache directory, or
replacing a cached file. IA-64 online update is refused because the reviewed
commit contains no corresponding object. JSON output includes the reviewed
repository commit, verified Git blob SHA-1, file SHA-256, and parsed summary.
.PP
Git SHA-1 is used only as the official repository object identifier for the
reviewed immutable file. It is not a general acquisition checksum or an
independent signature. The `authenticated_update_format` result means the file
has the expected UEFI authenticated-variable update structure; it does not
claim independent PKCS#7 signer-chain verification. Pin changes follow the
review ceremony in `docs/dbx-pin-refresh.md`.
.PP
.B dbx check
and
.B dbx scan
compare EFI Authenticode image hashes and embedded certificate bytes with a
selected DBX. They do not install the DBX or alter firmware state.
.SH UEFI MEDIA VALIDATION
.B uefi validate
performs a bounded descriptor-rooted read-only scan of mounted or extracted
media. It checks the architecture fallback loader, PE/EFI structure, optional
DBX image and certificate revocations, SBAT metadata, and trusted local or
running-firmware SBAT levels. It never modifies firmware or media.
.PP
.B uefi integrity manifest
creates exact uefi-md5sum-compatible manifest text from a bounded read-only
scan.
.B uefi integrity verify
checks the root `md5sum.txt` and reports changed, missing, unexpected, and byte
count mismatches. MD5 is used only for compatibility with the optional
boot-time validator; SHA-256 remains the trust primitive elsewhere.
.SH UEFI:NTFS ASSET INSPECTION
.B uefi-ntfs inspect
is a read-only structural inspection of the exact pinned 1 MiB Rufus 4.15
UEFI:NTFS FAT12 image. With no
.B --image
argument it locates the package asset; an explicit path must still match the
pinned size and whole-image SHA-256.
.PP
The command proves exactly five architecture triplets: ARM32, ARM64, IA32,
RISC-V64, and x64. Each triplet must contain its exact removable-media fallback
application plus NTFS and exFAT boot-service drivers. Every embedded path, file
size, SHA-256, PE/COFF machine, and subsystem is checked, and the deterministic
architecture manifest SHA-256 is reported. This validates the packaged bytes
and supported architecture set; it does not prove that physical firmware will
execute a loader or accept it under Secure Boot.
.PP
.SH WINDOWS SETUP ANALYSIS
Before optional Windows setup customizations, the identity-bound ISO is mounted
read-only and its complete installation metadata is inspected. Every WIM/ESD
edition must agree on Windows generation, client/server family, and
architecture. Existing split SWM sequences must be complete and unambiguous.
The graphical options summary reports bounded edition names/count, payload
kind, and part count. Unknown or conflicting metadata disables customizations
without blocking ordinary no-customization media creation.
.SH SAFETY
The program refuses partitions, read-only targets, the running root disk, and
an image stored on the selected target. It retains and hashes the selected
source, revalidates target identity immediately before destructive work, locks
the target, rejects unsafe symbolic-link traversal, flushes buffers, and checks
copied files, media structures, and filesystems. Cancellation leaves changed
incomplete media explicitly unqualified.
.PP
Software verification does not prove physical boot, persistence on untested
hardware, or Secure Boot compatibility for the unsigned package-owned
uefi-md5sum loader.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. A nonzero status indicates refusal, cancellation,
validation failure, I/O failure, filesystem failure, or verification mismatch.
